{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3223","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3223","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3223\",\"parent_revision\":\"dcac92e6f8817c11faf5228c67853b1ce71d8985\",\"root_revision\":\"268268d64e4ea070571e3b958b62a2930cc7c3de98caab6b0cafeb7b4027e331\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-24\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPR #3207 (plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review) added the `review-synthesizer` agent and a new T5 synthesis dispatch stage to the multi-perspective-review skill. `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` was left unchanged, so it still shows the obsolete four-worker topology with no `review-synthesizer`, `synthesis-worker`, or Punch List node.\\n\\nPer `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md`, this is a Tier 2 change (new agent dispatched, new Mermaid forks in a SKILL.md) requiring re-extraction of the G4 (concurrency/dispatch topology) and L0/L1 (forks/traces) layers before `assemble_graph.py` can rebuild the graph. Both COVERAGE.md and `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` state that single-pass extraction is prohibited (data must go through the 3-worker ensemble + `reduce.py` corroboration + sonnet-reducer assembly pattern) and that the dedicated `dh:workflow-extractor` agent that used to run this is retired, with re-extraction \\\"pending redesign\\\" (see `docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md`).\\n\\nBecause the extraction mechanism itself is pending redesign, this could not be done as part of PR #3207 without either hand-editing the layer JSON (explicitly prohibited by COVERAGE.md's \\\"What NOT to do\\\") or running an unvalidated single-pass extraction (explicitly prohibited by workflow-extraction.md's trust boundary rule).\\n\\nUser-provided context: once `dh:workflow-extractor`'s replacement exists (see the PRD), re-run it against `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` and `plugins/development-harness/agents/review-synthesizer.md` to regenerate G4 (and L0/L1 for the new forks), then run `uv run plugins/development-harness/docs/assemble_graph.py` to rebuild `dh-workflow-graph.json`.\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T16:00:40.385597Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: unbounded-design\\n\\n**Rationale**: The derived artifact `dh-workflow-graph.json` requires regeneration following PR #3207's source changes (new review-synthesizer agent + T5 stage). The work is not a behavioral defect (system functions correctly) nor a recurring failure pattern. The blocker is the incomplete design of the workflow-extractor tool itself, which is documented as \\\"pending redesign\\\" in `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` and the PRD. The mechanical rebuild task is deferred until the tool design exists to implement it and establish automated gates for future drift prevention.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: Decision tree traversal with prerequisite tracing to root cause.\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Tool design complete \u2192 automation gate enabled \u2192 artifact regeneration triggered on PR merge\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: PR #3207 review thread (chatgpt-codex-connector), addressed during rebase on 2026-08-24\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a2e74aa00abdc2adc462548d6c772a6f39a85944036e5de7b7382c862445d9dc\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRSXjcQ\"}"}